Code Red: the PokÉEG in the game (owner, 2026-10-09; brain scan 2026-10-10). A PC screen listing
every Pokémon the player owns (party, then the boxes) and, for the one under the cursor, a brain scan
built only from what it already is: five lobes (one per stat its nature touches; the raised one glows,
the lowered one dims), twelve electrodes (its IVs), four scrolling channels (BOND = friendship,
WIRING = IVs, TRAINING = EVs, MEMORY = its last ten turns of code), and seven tabs of text
(NATURE, WIRING, TRAINING, BOND, CODE, MEMORY, NOTE). Nature, IVs, EVs and friendship are read
here; its code memory comes from the page through a mailbox (struct CodeRedEeg, 264 B,
heap-allocated while the screen is open; the static symbol gCodeRedEeg is a pointer to it, NULL
when closed), one Pokémon at a time; hot memory is typed on the page. Display only.
Menu entries live in patch 003 (PC menu, bedroom PC); this patch is the screen itself.
No host → the game's own tabs still work; CODE/MEMORY/NOTE say to open the page.
